ffects.  Two exploratory signals remain unresolved but are not accepted. H6 for outcome_007 and feature_045 has a registered-direction point effect of about +0.014 signed, corresponding to a raw negative contrast of about -0.014, but the interval crosses zero and the point effect is only about 6% of the comparator mean, though the upper interval could approach a 10% relative difference. It is deferred. H8 for outcome_014 and feature_065 is more active: the signed estimate is +0.032, corresponding to raw feature_065-positive minus comparator of about -0.032, i.e. stronger dependency, and this is a large relative effect compared with the near-zero comparator mean for outcome_014. However, the 95% interval crosses zero, outcome_014 has high variance, and relative percentage effects on an outcome with a mean near zero are numerically unstable. H8 remains active but unresolved.  The most informative next analysis is to test whether the H8 signal is internally consistent in strata defined by a balanced untested binary marker, feature_002. H14 and H15 estimate the feature_065 effect on outcome_014 within feature_002-positive and feature_002-negative eligible cells. If both strata show consistent negative raw contrasts with intervals excluding zero and clinically meaningful magnitude, that will support requesting independent validation. If only one stratum is positive, this suggests heterogeneity or confounding. If both are null or narrow, H8 should be downgraded or closed. I would deprioritize further feature_006 follow-up unless an adjusted or independent design can address the discovery-validation discrepancy.  All conclusions are limited to associations in the supplied dataset. Predictor labels are opaque, unadjusted contrasts may be confounded by correlated predictors, and no causal or generalizability claim is supported without independent replication and more adjusted modeling.",
